verification.reason:
Confirmed, with one claim narrowed. At b6fca69, main_help in src/bin/mhfe/main.rs still types three command summaries as string literals instead of using their constants:
- main.rs:170 repeats rekey::SUMMARY (rekey.rs:110);
- main.rs:172 repeats wallets::SUMMARY (wallets.rs:34);
- main.rs:175 repeats container_repair::REPAIR_SUMMARY (container_repair.rs:128).

The `mhfe new` row (main.rs:149) is the only one that uses its constant. Commit 253ca3c changed that one row, the one AUD-023-ARC006 named, and left the other three copies of the same root cause. That breaches CORE-10 ("the same ... message is built in one place"; "a copy found while working is merged in the same change"). The copies gate says in its header that it leaves "a constant written in many places" to review, and no test looks at main_help. My harness exits 1 and lists exactly these three copies, and the rendered --help shows the same texts.

What I refuted is that the check row "has already drifted". "Rehearse a recovery without showing the phrase" (main.rs:162) and the summary "...without ever showing the phrase" have both stood unchanged since cc91b0b. git log -S shows that neither text was ever edited toward or away from the other. That row is also one of five plain-command examples that paraphrase their summary on purpose (encrypt, decrypt, check, password, self-test), so it is not a copy. I took it out of the defect and changed the title and fields to match. Severity stays low: the risk is wording drift, nothing behaves wrongly.

